# BogenTrack UI

Before building or restyling UI, read `docs/DESIGN.md`.

## Tokens and widgets

- Colors, spacing, radius, typography, motion: `lib/core/theme/` — never hardcode colors, font sizes, or padding.
- Screen shells, cards, buttons, scores: `lib/core/widgets/` — do not reinvent patterns.

## Cross-platform rules

- Identical look on iOS and Android.
- `google_fonts` only (Newsreader + Inter) — never system/default fonts.
- Cupertino widgets on both platforms: `CupertinoButton`, `CupertinoSwitch`, `CupertinoPicker`, `showCupertinoModalPopup`, `CupertinoSlidingSegmentedControl`.
- Never `*.adaptive`, `showAdaptiveDialog`, or `Theme.of` / `Platform` branches for styling.
- No Material ink ripple — use `AppButton` or `CupertinoButton` with fade feedback.

## Scores

Use `ScoreText` (or `FontFeature.tabularFigures()`) for **every** score, average, and total numeral.

## Scope

Visual and interaction design only — do not change scoring logic, domain models, or persistence unless explicitly requested.

## When changing the design system

Update `docs/DESIGN.md` and `lib/core/theme/` in the same PR.
